    <statement><p>Let <m>\displaystyle f(x)= \frac{6 \sin x}{2 \sin x + 4 \cos x}</m>.</p>
<p>Then <m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
<p>The equation of the tangent line to <m>y=f(x)</m> at <m>a = \pi/3</m> can be written in the form <m>y=mx+b</m> where</p>
<p><m>m =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> and</p>
<p><m>b =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/>.</p>
</statement>
